iew before you merge\nL827: \nL828: Inspect the summary and diff, request a follow-up, or open a pull request when the result is ready.\nL829: \nL830: Quickstart\nL831: \nL832: ## Set up Codex cloud\nL833: \nL834: Connect GitHub or GitLab, create an environment, and start your first cloud chat.\nL835: \nL836:   1. 1\nL837: ### Open Codex and sign in\nL838: \nL839: Go to cite432†Codex†chatgpt.com and sign in with your ChatGPT account.\nL840: \nL841:   2. 2\nL842: \nL843: ### Connect GitHub or GitLab\nL844: \nL845: Connect GitHub or GitLab (Beta) when prompted. For GitHub, choose the repositories Codex can access; for GitLab, select a project when you create the environment.\nL846: \nL847: For GitLab setup, webhook permissions, and merge request reviews, see cite310†Use Codex with GitLab (Beta) .\nL848: \nL849:   3. 3\nL850: ### Create an environment\nL851: \nL852: Open cite434†environment settings†chatgpt.com and create an environment for the repository you selected. Configure any dependencies, tools, environment variables, or secrets the task needs.\nL853: \nL854: For configuration details, see cite302†Cloud environments .\nL855: \nL856:   4. 4\nL857: \nL858: ### Start your first task\nL859: \nL860: Return to cite432†Codex†chatgpt.com , choose your environment, and describe the result you want. You can watch the task logs or let the task run in the background.\nL861: \nL862:   5. 5\nL863: ### Review the result\nL864: \nL865: Review the summary and diff. Ask Codex to make follow-up changes, or open a pull request when the work is ready.\nL866: \nL867: Next steps\nL868: \nL869:   * cite302†Customize the cloud environment L870:   * cite320†Configure agent internet access L871:   * cite309†Use Codex with GitHub L872:   * cite310†Use Codex with GitLab (Beta) L873:   * cite312†Use Codex in Linear L874:   * cite311†Use Codex in Slack L875: \nL876: ## See what Codex cloud can do\nL877: \nL878: Give each task the environment it needs, then re